codex
The definedness lemma alone does not stop evaluator branching. I’m removing it and introducing a named reverse summary whose meaning is fixed in a separate bridge-free module by the exact frozen `buildVS` term. The target module contains only the inverse orientation; the connection proof is compiled without that orientation, so the summary cannot float free of the supplied semantics.
